  "notes": [
   "The SEN136B5B has a single SIG pin; the catalogue hc-sr04 has separate TRIG and ECHO, so SIG is modelled on TRIG and ECHO is unused.",
   "The breadboard columns are read from the image: the sensor pins are in columns 9, 10 and 11 (GND, 5V, SIG) in row h of the upper half (bank b, rows f-j). The jumper wires are in row g of the same columns.",
   "The image shows the GND wire on the Uno header pin beside AREF. I assigned it to GND.1 because the catalogue does not say which GND that is.",
   "The tutorial has no resistors or LEDs, so none are added."
  ]
